# GenericDbContext: Dynamic Entity Registration

## Class Declaration

The `GenericDbContext` inherits from `DbContext` and accepts dependencies for configuration, assembly scanning, and HTTP context access:

```csharp
public class GenericDbContext : DbContext
{
    private readonly AssemblyService assemblyService;
    private readonly IHttpContextAccessor context;
    private readonly IDatabaseProviderConfiguration dbConfigProvider;
    private readonly IConfiguration config;
```

## Model Building Strategy

The `OnModelCreating` method implements a two-phase entity discovery approach:

**Phase 1 - Configuration Classes:**
```csharp
foreach (var asm in this.assemblyService.Assemblies)
{
    builder.ApplyConfigurationsFromAssembly(asm);
}
```

This applies all `IEntityTypeConfiguration` implementations found in discovered assemblies.

**Phase 2 - Unmapped Types:**
```csharp
foreach (var customType in this.assemblyService.Types.Where(x => 
    !x.IsAssignableFrom(typeof(IEntityTypeConfiguration<>))))
{
    builder.Entity(customType);
}
```

Any entities without explicit configurations are automatically registered.

## Tenant Filtering

The code applies query filters to multi-tenant entities:

```csharp
foreach (var customType in this.assemblyService.Types.Where(x => 
    x.IsAssignableFrom(typeof(IHasTenantId))))
{
    var tenant = this.context.HttpContext.GetUser().TenantId;
    builder.Entity(customType).HasQueryFilter((IHasTenantId p) => 
        p.TenantId == tenant);
}
```

## Notable Omissions

The code contains commented-out trigger and async save methods, suggesting these features were previously used but are currently disabled. No explicit migration, `EnsureCreated`, or schema update mechanisms appear in this file.

