24	    ///
25	    /// <para><b>Antiforgery is global and it is not optional.</b> A generated application
26	    /// authenticates the browser with a cookie, which means the browser attaches it to any request
27	    /// any page can provoke — so every state-changing verb needs a token the attacker's page cannot
28	    /// read. <see cref="AutoValidateAntiforgeryTokenAttribute"/> as a global filter covers POST, PUT,
29	    /// PATCH and DELETE across every controller, including ones added later by hand. Applying it per
30	    /// controller instead would work exactly until somebody adds a controller and does not know to,
31	    /// and that failure is silent from the inside — the endpoint works perfectly, for everybody,
32	    /// including the page that forged the request.</para>
33	    /// </summary>
