23	/// <para><b>Pages are expanded, not interpreted.</b> A block tree could be handed to a renderer that
24	/// walks it at runtime, and that would be less code here. It would also mean a person who wants to
25	/// change a screen has nothing to edit: the page would be data, and the only way to alter it would
26	/// be to alter the definition. Expanding the tree into a real component means the generated file is
27	/// a Vue file — readable, diffable, breakpoint-able, and yours to change once you stop
28	/// regenerating it.</para>
